From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] args: fix missing <cstdint> include for uint64_t

Upstream-Status: To upstream [not yet submitted; python-wheels does not open issues/PRs on third-party repos]

args.cc uses `uint64_t` in `getAutotuneModelSize()` without including
`<cstdint>`, relying on it being pulled in transitively by another
header. GCC 13 stopped exposing it that way
(https://gcc.gnu.org/gcc-13/porting_to.html#header-dep-changes), so the
build fails with any GCC >= 13, including the manylinux_riscv64 image's,
and reproduces on x86_64 with Ubuntu 24.04's GCC 13.3:

    src/args.cc:512:3: error: 'uint64_t' was not declared in this scope

floret is a fork of fastText, which fixed the same line in
facebookresearch/fastText@6c2204ba66776b700095ff73e3e599a908ffd9c3
("fix compile error with gcc13 #1281 (#1340)"); floret has not picked
it up, including on its main branch.

Signed-off-by: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
---
 src/args.cc | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/src/args.cc b/src/args.cc
index a8975e8..8dd2232 100644
--- a/src/args.cc
+++ b/src/args.cc
@@ -9,6 +9,7 @@
 #include "args.h"
 
 #include <stdlib.h>
+#include <cstdint>
 
 #include <iostream>
 #include <stdexcept>
